    "content": "Materials: Blank table on board or worksheet: 'Number A' | 'Number B' | 'Hundreds Compare' | 'Tens Compare' | 'Ones Compare' | 'Final Symbol'. How to do it: 1) Draw a 6-column table on the board. 2) Write 742 and 724 in first two columns. 3) Ask: 'Compare hundreds: 7 vs 7. Same or different?' (Same) — Write 'Same' in column 3. 4) Ask: 'Move to tens: 4 vs 2. Which is bigger?' (4 > 2) — Write '4 > 2' in column 4. 5) Say: 'We found a difference at tens place. So final symbol: 742 > 724.' 6) Students complete 4 more rows independently.",
