    "keyConcept": "'Left to Right, Stop at First Difference' Rule",
    "content": "Materials: Whiteboard, markers, anchor chart. How to do it: 1) Write on board: RULE: Compare left to right (Hundreds → Tens → Ones). STOP at the first place where digits are different. The bigger digit there decides the whole comparison. 2) Model: 742 vs 724 — Hundreds: 7 vs 7 (same — keep going), Tens: 4 vs 2 (different — STOP!), 4 > 2, so 3) > 724. 4) Model again: 845 vs 849 — Hundreds: 8 vs 8 (same), Tens: 4 vs 4 (same), Ones: 5 vs 9 (different — 5) STOP!), 5 < 9, so 845 < 849. 6) Students chant the rule aloud 3 times.",
