    "keyConcept": "Bundles & Borrow with Base-10 Blocks",
    "content": "Materials: Base-10 blocks (flats=100, rods=10, units=1), place value mat, subtraction cards. How to do it: 1) Show 500 – 275 on the board. 2) Give a student: 5 flats (500). Arrange on mat: Hundreds | Tens | Ones. 3) Say: 'We need to subtract 275. That means remove 2 hundreds, 7 tens, 5 ones.' 4) Try to remove 5 ones: 'No ones! Borrow 1 ten from tens place. But tens place has 0!' 5) Say: 'So borrow 1 hundred from hundreds. 1 hundred = 10 tens.' 6) Exchange: 5 hundreds → 4 hundreds + 10 tens. Then borrow 1 ten → 9 tens + 10 ones. 7) Now remove: 2 hundreds, 7 tens, 5 ones. Left: 2 hundreds, 2 tens, 5 ones = 225. 8) Repeat with 600 – 345, 800 – 488.",
