    "keyConcept": "Borrowing Tracking Table",
    "content": "Materials: Blank table on board or worksheet: 'Number' | 'Hundreds' | 'Tens' | 'Ones' | 'After Borrowing' | 'Answer'. How to do it: 1) Draw a 6-column table on the board. 2) Write 500 in first column. Fill: Hundreds=5, Tens=0, Ones=0. 3) Write 275 below as 'to subtract'. 4) Ask: 'Can we subtract 5 ones from 0 ones?' (No → borrow) 5) Track borrowing: Borrow 1 hundred → Hundreds become 4, Tens become 10. Then borrow 1 ten → Tens become 9, Ones become 10. 6) Write 'After Borrowing': 4 | 9 | 10. 7) Subtract: 4−2=2 hundreds, 9−7=2 tens, 10−5=5 ones → 225. 8) Students complete 4 more rows independently.",
