    "keyConcept": "Real Pencil Shop",
    "content": "Materials: Real pencils (or objects), play money (£1 coins or notes). How to do it: 1) Place 2 pencils on a desk. Next to them put a sign: '£10 for 2 pencils'. 2) Give a student £10 in play money. Ask: 'If you buy both pencils, how much money do you give me?' (Take the £10). 3) Now say: 'You have 2 pencils. You want to know the cost of 1 pencil. Put the £10 back and share it equally between the 2 pencils.' 4) Student counts out £5 for each pencil. Repeat with different students and different totals (e.g. £8 for 2 pencils).",
