    "keyConcept": "Sides = Angles Rule",
    "content": "Materials: Worksheets with 5 different polygons (including concave and irregular), counting space. How to do it: 1) Write on the board: 'Every polygon has ______ sides and ______ angles.' 2) Students test 5 shapes: for each, they count sides and count angles, then fill in the blanks. 3) After testing, they write the rule: 'For any polygon, the number of sides equals the number of angles.' 4) Class discusses: 'Did any shape break the rule?' (No — it's always true.) 5) Ask: 'Why does this happen?' (Because each side ends at a corner, and each corner is an angle.)",
