    "content": "Materials: Simple drawn or described image of a dining table; Paper and pencil. How to do it: 1) Show the image or read the description aloud. 2) Ask: 'Who is missing? Why?' (Grandparent who passed away, parent working late, sibling in another city, someone who is sick.) 3) Students write 2 possible inferences for who the empty chair belongs to. 4) Then ask: 'When did you miss someone at a meal? Who were they? Why weren't they there?' 5) Optional: Students draw their own 'empty chair' and write the name of who they miss.",
