    "keyConcept": "The Silenced Sentence",
    "content": "Materials: One line of dialogue written on board; Sticky notes or small slips of paper. How to do it: 1) Read the line aloud with a specific tone (angry, sad, or tired). 2) Ask: 'What did the character NOT say? What is the hidden sentence?' (Example: 'Fine' = 'I am not fine at all. You hurt me.') 3) Students write the silenced sentence on a sticky note. 4) Share 3–4 examples with the class. 5) Personal connection: 'I once said fine but really wanted to say…' 6) Discuss: 'Why do people say fine when they are not fine?'",
