    "content": "Materials: 'Fish' cards (word on one side), fishing rods made from rulers and string with a paperclip hook, bucket. How to do it: 1) Spread fish cards face-down in the 'pond' (a bucket or taped area on the floor). 2) Students take turns 'fishing' — pick up a card and read the word. 3) If it is a noun: keep the fish and say its category. If not: throw it back. 4) Player with the most fish at the end wins. 5) Debrief: which words were the trickiest? Why?",
