    "keyConcept": "Noun Auction",
    "content": "Materials: List of 20 words on the board (mix of nouns and non-nouns), each student gets 10 'coins' (counters or paper tokens). How to do it: 1) Explain the rules: students bid their coins to 'buy' words they believe are nouns. 2) Teacher 'auctions' each word — students bid by raising their hand and stating an amount (1–3 coins). 3) Highest bidder wins the word. If it IS a noun: they keep it. If NOT: they lose their coins. 4) After all 20 words, count each student's remaining coins plus won noun cards. 5) Richest student wins. Debrief every non-noun that was mistakenly bought.",
